# Lecture Notes

Two proof-focused manuscripts are maintained:

- `Lecture draft/Lecture draft.tex`: the b-calculus, Fredholm theory on
  closed manifolds and cylindrical ends, the APS spectral boundary problem,
  and K-theoretic and heat-kernel proofs of the Atiyah--Patodi--Singer theorem.
- `Lecture draft/Atiyah-Singer index theorem.tex`: elliptic operators,
  K-theoretic push-forward, heat kernels, Clifford modules, the local index
  theorem, Gauss--Bonnet, the signature theorem, almost Hermitian and almost
  Kähler geometry, the almost Dolbeault operator, and Riemann--Roch.

The July 2026 revision is a line-by-line mathematical edit of the original
lecture transcriptions. Relevant classroom discussion is retained as concise
Discussion and Question/Answer interludes; speaker attributions, unresolved
chatter, duplicated chapters, generated files, and unrelated archive material
are omitted. Definitions precede use, theorem hypotheses are explicit, and
proof gaps are filled or identified as standard input. The original diagrams
were audited against the surrounding arguments, then redrawn and consolidated
as captioned, reproducible TikZ figures; additional diagrams mark the symbol,
blow-up, spectral, parametrix, and heat-kernel constructions where the geometry
is easier to see than to infer from formulas alone.

## Build

From `Lecture draft/`:

```sh
latexmk -pdf -interaction=nonstopmode -halt-on-error "Lecture draft.tex"
latexmk -pdf -interaction=nonstopmode -halt-on-error "Atiyah-Singer index theorem.tex"
```

Both manuscripts build with pdfLaTeX. Build products are intentionally
untracked.
